WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:04.509
Its been about a month since I got my shiny
new airPods 2 with wireless charging, I’ve

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:08.160
been using them almost every day, as a replacement
to the original airPods that I’ve owned

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.280
and loved since they were released over 3
years ago.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.440
So what's the vedict, was it worth upgrading
and spending $200+ Tax?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:21.340
To be honest, for me, no not really, but there
is one group of people who they do make sense

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.910
for, but I’ll cover that in a bit.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.360
Coming up to launch of these new Airpods there
quite a bit of rumors.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.450
Health tracking features, sweat resistance,
really fast wireless charging, and new colors.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.359
None of that came true and a lot of people
were upset.

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:40.739
Airpods are everywhere and they had most people
love them, They even got a 98% customer satisfaction

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.250
rating which is really good.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.710
It makes sense that people which is understandable
since over three years later we want some

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.809
of these great additions.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:49.579
I personally would have loved getting them
in black.

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:54.730
What we got was some minor updates, wireless
charging if you spend $200, hey Siri support,

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.600
and a new H1 chip.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.809
To be honest I wasn’t really interested
in wireless charging since I rarely have to

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:07.561
charge the case compared to a phone but it
was quite convient to just drop them onto

00:01:07.561 --> 00:01:13.230
my qi pad when I get home instead of on my
nightstand, that way I never feel like I actually

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.230
have to change them.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.770
With that said wireless charging is really
slow.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:20.820
They accept 5 watts just like your standard
iPhone brick but take almost twice as long

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.590
to charge because wireless charging is less
efficient.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:30.610
Them side by side and after 10min Airpods
2 only gained 8% wirelessly while my original

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.200
plugged in gained 20%.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.500
I figured we wouldn’t get any sound improvements
since Apple didn't mention it and I was already

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.230
happy with the sound for an unsealed earbud.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.700
One thing I was looking forward to is faster
and more reliable connections with the new

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.890
H1 chip and better range with BT5.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:52.740
The H1 chip does connect noticeably faster
and slightly more reliably as well.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.450
One issue I had in the past was swapping Airpods
from my iPhone to my Mac.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.670
It would take a while and sometimes I would
have to hit connect another time.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.920
Airpods 2 is faster and more reliable but
its not perfect, with that said even a month

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.790
later i’m often shocked how fast they can
connect.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:08.790
We did a full comparison testing a bunch of
things between them, so if you want to check

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.790
out that detailed video you can click here
or the box after this video.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:13.290
H1 also has less latency but its you can’t
notice it for music and videos since the iPhone

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.599
will wait to sync up, but this is noticeable
in games.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:20.319
As for range, it's not really better any better.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:25.800
Sometimes I leave my phone on the charger
playing podcasts or music while doing some

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.800
work outside.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.930
If I get halfway down my driveway it cuts
out and same thing for most of my garage so

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.840
I was really hoping for some improvement.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.019
Looking at Bluetooth 5 specs the range is
rated quite a bit longer but in my testing,

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:43.099
it was practically the same, well to specific
I got 3 feet further.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:45.159
Last, let's touch on Hey Siri.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:49.310
I’ve used it a few times when I didn’t
have my watch and it works quite well.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.650
Delay is minimal and it's definitely better
than having to double tap to envoke siri.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.709
If you don’t have an Apple watch and want
to have hands free control this could be a

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:02.190
legit reason to upgrade but personally for
me it's quicker just to spin my watch crown

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.599
to adjust volume or lift my wrist and ask
a question without having to say that special

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:07.599
phrase.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:12.430
I mentioned one group of people that upgrading
to Airpods 2 make sense.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.989
Those that bought Airpods close to launch
and have used them a lot since then.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:22.420
I was surprised reading quite a bit of comment
from those saying the batteries in their originals

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.769
are now half of what they used to be, and
since they love them so much they have no

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:29.480
problems upgrading.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.900
If you don’t need wireless charging, and
I would argue most dont you can refresh your

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.280
pair with a newer version thats faster, more
reliable, and with hey Siri for the same price

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.560
as before.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.700
Actually possibly cheaper now that Amazon
officially sells them and has had a few sales

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.459
for $140, We’ll leave a link in the description.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:49.730
So overall these small updates are an improvement
but for most people, unless your battery if

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:54.230
dead or you can really benefit from hey Siri,
upgrading to airpods 2 isn’t worth it.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.200
Thank you guys for watching if you guys want
to see more videos like this one click the

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.230
card above to subscribe and check out our
airpods1 vs 2 detailed comparisons or are

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:12.470
Galaxy buds worth it for iPhone users.

